            <ArticleTitle>Percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty in a patient with paroxysmal nocturnal hemoglobinuria.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>144-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Paroxysmal nocturnal hemoglobinuria (PHN) is an acquired chronic hemolytic anemia associated with an unusual susceptibility to hemolytic crisis, infection, and venous thrombosis which would be aggravated by a number of factors including surgery. We report a case of PHN undergoing percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty and discuss the corresponding perioperative management.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
